        "Mandatory aggregator duties that the platform performs and does not exclude. Regardless of the payment model, to the extent the platform qualifies as an aggregator owner it: (a) provides consumers with information about itself (business name, location (address), business hours, OGRN/OGRNIP) and an email address; (b) enables the cook-seller to post accurate information about itself needed to conclude and perform the contract and to bring claims (Art. 9 of the Consumer Protection Law); (c) is liable for the consumer's losses caused by the provision of FALSE or incomplete information ABOUT THE GOODS OR THE SELLER conveyed by the platform (Art. 12(2.1)), provided that the platform is not liable where such information was received from the cook-seller unchanged and the platform did not know and should not have known of its inaccuracy. These duties are mandatory and are not limited by the disclaimers of liability in this document.",
        "Introducing prepayment in the future. If and when the platform begins accepting advance payment for goods from consumers through the platform, the duties of an aggregator owner that has accepted prepayment apply to it in full, including the duty to refund the advance payment to a consumer who has refused the goods where the goods are not delivered within the time stipulated by the contract, within 10 (ten) days of the demand (Art. 12(2.2) and (4)). Users will be notified of such a change in advance, and the current terms will be posted on the platform.",
